I recieved this game from a friend, because it was a game-give-away night. Also, this is one of the very few RPGs I've played
.
Absolutely amazing story. I loved it all the way through, and I wish it was made into a novel as I feel that would be a slightly better format for it. The music is also very well done; it sets a great tone and emotion for scenes and experiences. The choice system is kind of crazy (which is why it would be hard to make a novel out of it.. hah), and some choices have more significance over others (they keep bringing up one in particular that would seem very, very minor), and some have consequences that you didn't see coming at all or could've be spelled out more (
), but over all well done, and can help teach you who you are...
Puzzles were very (
) annoying at times, animations can be quite wonky, graphics aren't very well optimized (but they are there; it doesn't look like crap!), but overall... the music and story is what makes it. Dunno if I'd buy it full priced, but if it's on sale.. grab it for the story.

I loved The Longest Journey and I was looking forward to an awesome sequel... but I was dissapointed.
- the puzzels were way too easy (press this, go there, done);
- they forgot they are making a game -> my input as a player was close to nothing;
Basically it's worth playing only if you loved TLJ and want to know how the story ends (at least the story lived up to my expectations).

